2️⃣ Open MongoDB Shell

Press Windows + R

Type:

mongosh


Press Enter

Press Enter again when it asks for connection string

You should now see:

test>


This is where we type commands.

3️⃣ STEP-BY-STEP COMMANDS (TYPE EXACTLY)
🔹 STEP 1: Create / Switch to Database

Type:

use collegeDB


Output:

switched to db collegeDB


📌 Database is created automatically when data is added.

🔹 STEP 2: Create Collection & Insert ONE Document

Type:

db.students.insertOne({
  name: "Lohitha",
  roll: 4,
  branch: "CSE"
})


Output:

acknowledged: true


📌 Collection students is created automatically.

🔹 STEP 3: Insert MULTIPLE Documents

Type:

db.students.insertMany([
  { name: "Anu", roll: 102, branch: "IT" },
  { name: "Khushil", roll: 103, branch: "ECE" }
])

🔹 STEP 4: Read (Display) Data

Type:

db.students.find()


You’ll see all records printed.

🔹 STEP 5: Update a Document

Update branch of roll 101:

db.students.updateOne(
  { roll: 101 },
  { $set: { branch: "AI" } }
)

🔹 STEP 6: Verify Update
db.students.find({ roll: 101 })

🔹 STEP 7: Delete a Document
db.students.deleteOne({ roll: 103 })

🔹 STEP 8: Verify Delete
db.students.find()

4️⃣ OTHER IMPORTANT COMMANDS (FOR EXAM)
Show all databases:
show dbs

Show collections in current DB:
show collections

Drop collection:
db.students.drop()

Drop database:
db.dropDatabase()
